Confirmed: `uint8_t key[0];` — a **zero-length array**! So `sizeof(ext.key) == 0` → the app's clamp `if (ext.key_len > sizeof(ext.key)) ext.key_len = 0;` sets key_len to **0** and copies nothing. **That's the bug.**

Fix in the app: don't clamp to `sizeof(ext.key)`. Use a properly sized buffer:
```c
struct
{
  struct iw_encode_ext ext;
  char key[128];
} enc;

memset(&enc, 0, sizeof(enc));
enc.ext.alg = IW_ENCODE_ALG_CCMP;
enc.ext.key_len = strlen(psk);
if (enc.ext.key_len > sizeof(enc.key)) enc.ext.key_len = sizeof(enc.key);
memcpy(enc.key, psk, enc.ext.key_len);
iwr.u.encoding.pointer = &enc.ext;
iwr.u.encoding.length = sizeof(enc.ext) + enc.ext.key_len;
iwr.u.encoding.flags = IW_ENCODE_INDEX;
```
