Found it: `connect(fd, ...)` is **blocking** with no timeout. If ai_agent isn't listening (or the IP is unreachable), the TCP connect can hang for a long time (NuttX's default connect timeout / retries).

Fix: make the connect **non-blocking with a bounded poll** (e.g. 1500 ms):
```c
fd = socket(...);
fcntl(fd, F_SETFL, O_NONBLOCK);
rc = connect(fd, ...);
if (rc < 0 && errno != EINPROGRESS) { close; return -errno; }
if (rc < 0) {
   poll(POLLOUT, 1500ms);
   getsockopt(SO_ERROR) to check;
}
fcntl(fd, F_SETFL, blocking);   /* 后续 WS 收发按阻塞语义 */
```
